Homepage: https://github.com/Open-Mixer/omx-contract
Description: one shared source of truth for every OpenMixer knob, range, default
 A fader range, a default, a plugin parameter, a supported sample rate: in
 OpenMixer each of these is written down once, in omx-contract, and everything
 else reads it. That is why the console, the DSP library and the plugins agree
 on what a knob does and how far it turns. The declarations are plain JSON with
 a JSON Schema, so tools in any language can read them, and they are rendered
 as C headers for the code that is built from them.
 .
 This package holds the c render under /usr/include/omxcontract,
 omx-contract.pc and install-contract-dir.sh, which an owner's build
 installs its definitions with. The data it builds against is
 omx-contract-data, which it depends on. A consumer requires it at a floor,
 the lowest release whose declarations it builds against.
 .
 Its documentation is on openmixer.org.

